{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785260916,"nonce":"N85RYlYL/aLJo+vAx3z2XWDiu2M=","title":"ADR-0064 s2: prove the cold tier by st_dev, degrade gracefully without one, and stamp durability on the Attempt","message":"\"Durable\" is a property of the **backing**, not of the tier's name. `StoreConfig::LocalDir` may point at the warm volume itself, or at the Helm chart's `scratch` **emptyDir** — in which case \"written to cold\" licenses nothing, and the word \"cold\" implies a promise nothing is making.\n\nThe test is `st_dev` of the cold directory against the warm directory. **\"Is it object storage?\" is the wrong test**: it rejects a second PVC (a perfectly good cold tier) and cannot detect a `LocalDir` sitting beside the CAS.\n\n| cold | verdict |\n|---|---|\n| S3/MinIO | genuine second tier |\n| `LocalDir` on a separate volume | `st_dev` differs → genuine tier |\n| `LocalDir` on the warm volume | same → **not a tier** |\n| `LocalDir` on the chart `emptyDir` | same, and dies with the Pod |\n\nWhere there is no independent tier the Depot **degrades rather than refusing** (ADR-0061: object storage is \"an operator's cost decision, not an engine decision\"), and the weaker guarantee is disclosed.\n\n- [ ] `st_dev` comparison at startup; a second PVC counts as a real tier\n- [ ] Warm-only is a supported configuration, stated loudly at startup — not a refusal, and not a silent downgrade\n- [ ] The durability tier that backed a snapshot is **stamped on the Attempt** beside `output_snapshot`/`output_identity` (new column) — a startup log cannot explain a Run a month later, and deployments gain an S3 bucket while their old records do not change\n- [ ] The UI can say \"this Run's evidence was never archived; this deployment had no independent durable tier\" instead of showing a mystery gap","files":null}]}